exercises.solutionCode:
-- Fix: use SET LOCAL instead of SET, so the setting is automatically
-- scoped to just this transaction and reverted at COMMIT/ROLLBACK.
BEGIN;
SET LOCAL search_path = tenant_x;
SELECT * FROM orders LIMIT 5;
COMMIT;
-- connection returned to the pool with search_path back to its default --
-- no tenant-specific state survives past this transaction.

-- Defense in depth: configure PgBouncer's server_reset_query
-- (e.g. DISCARD ALL) so any OTHER session state is also scrubbed
-- before a connection is handed to the next client, regardless of
-- whether every code path remembered to use SET LOCAL correctly.
